  "steps": [
    "To a blender, add ½ cup (65g) cashews, ½ cup (120g) coconut cream, 2 tbsp honey, A pinch of salt. Blend until smooth, transfer the mixture to a lined container and refrigerate for at least 1 hour, or until firm.",
    "Once the base is ready, it’s time to make the caramel layer. In a bowl, combine ½ cup (130g) peanut butter, 2 tbsp honey, 1 tsp vanilla extract. Pour the mixture over the chilled base and sprinkle a handful of roasted peanuts on top.",
    "Freeze for at least 1 hour, then remove it from the container and cut it into 4 bars.",
    "Coat each bar in melted dark chocolate - preferably 70% cocoa or higher. You’ll need approximately 150g of chocolate to coat all four bars.",
    "Sprinkle a little salt on top. The chocolate will harden almost instantly when it comes into contact with the frozen bars.",
    "Your homemade Snickers bars are ready!"
  ],
